===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*bʰer-}}
From {{inh|en|enm|difference}}, from {{der|en|fro|difference}}, from {{der|en|la|differentia|t=difference}}, from {{m|la|differēns|t=different}}, present participle of {{m|la|differo|differre}}. {{doublet|en|differentia}}.

Morphologically {{suffix|en|differ|ence|nocat=1}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈdɪf(ə)ɹəns/}}
* {{audio|en|En-us-difference.ogg|Audio (US)}}
* {{audio|en|En-au-difference.ogg|Audio (AU)}}
* {{hyph|en|diffe|rence}}, {{hyph|en|dif|fer|ence|nocaption=1}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{lb|en|uncountable}} The quality of being [[different]].
#: {{ant|en|identity|sameness}}
#: {{ux|en|You need to learn to be more tolerant of '''difference'''.}}
# {{lb|en|countable}} A characteristic of something that makes it different from something else.
#: {{ux|en|There are three '''differences''' between these two pictures.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|title=Towards the end of poverty| date=2013-06-01| volume=407| issue=8838| page=11| magazine=w:The Economist| url=http://www.economist.com/news/leaders/21578665-nearly-1-billion-people-have-been-taken-out-extreme-poverty-20-years-world-should-aim| passage=But poverty’s scourge is fiercest below $1.25 (the average of the 15 poorest countries’ own poverty lines, measured in 2005 dollars and adjusted for '''differences''' in purchasing power): people below that level live lives that are poor, nasty, brutish and short.}}
# {{lb|en|countable}} A [[disagreement]] or [[argument]].
#: {{ux|en|We have our little '''differences''', but we are firm friends.}}
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Cymbeline|I|v|passage=What was the '''difference'''? It was a contention in public.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1714|author=w:Thomas Ellwood|title= The History of the Life of Thomas Ellwood: written by his own hand
|passage=Away therefore went I with the constable, leaving the old warden and the young constable to compose their '''difference''' as they could.}}
# {{lb|en|countable|uncountable}} Significant change in or effect on a situation or state.
#: {{ux|en|It just won't make much '''difference''' to me.}}
#: {{ux|en|It just won't make much of a '''difference''' to anyone.}}
#* {{RQ:Grahame Wind in the Willows|passage=The line of the horizon was clear and hard against the sky, and in one particular quarter it showed black against a silvery climbing [[phosphorescence]] that grew and grew. At last, over the rim of the waiting earth the moon lifted with slow majesty till it swung clear of the horizon and rode off, free of [[moorings]]; and once more they began to see surfaces&mdash;meadows wide-spread, and quiet gardens, and the river itself from bank to bank, all softly [[disclosed]], all washed clean of mystery and terror, all radiant again as by day, but with a '''difference''' that was tremendous.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1967|author=w:Barbara Sleigh| title=w:Jessamy| year_published=1993| location=Sevenoaks, Kent| publisher=Bloomsbury| isbn=0 340 19547 9| page=105| passage=As she did so Fanny put down her book , stood up and stretched her arms, and at once Jessamy noticed a '''difference'''. It was the same Fanny but not the Fanny who climbed trees and tore her frock playing in the garden. It was as though a young lady film had settled over her, neatening her unruly hair, which was tied back with a large black bow, and primly composing her small mouth.}}
# {{senseid|en|subtraction}} {{lb|en|countable}} The result of a [[subtraction]]; sometimes the [[absolute value]] of this result.
#: {{ux|en|The '''difference''' between 3 and 21 is 18.}}
# {{lb|en|obsolete}} Choice; preference.
#* {{RQ:Spenser Faerie Queene|book=II|canto=XII|passage=That now be chooseth with vile '''difference''' <br> To be a beast, and lack intelligence.}}
# {{lb|en|heraldry}} An addition to a [[coat of arms]] to distinguish two people's [[bearing]]s which would otherwise be the same. See {{m|en|augmentation}} and {{m|en|cadency}}.
# {{lb|en|logic}} The quality or attribute which is added to those of the [[genus]] to constitute a [[species]]; a [[differentia]].
# {{lb|en|logic circuits}} A [[Boolean]] operation which is [[true]] when the two input variables are different but is otherwise [[false]]; the [[XOR]] operation (<math>\scriptstyle A \overline B + \overline A B</math>).
# {{lb|en|relational algebra}} The [[set]] of [[element]]s that are in one set but not another (<math>\scriptstyle A \overline B</math>).

